# Phase 7: Options Calculator — ML-Powered Pricing Engine

## Overview

Add a complete Options Calculator to PaperTick with three pricing engines running in parallel:
1. **Black-Scholes** (analytical baseline)
2. **Monte Carlo** (10K simulations with antithetic variates)
3. **Hybrid LSTM-CNN** (neural network with physics-informed loss, falls back to noisy BS when untrained)

Results are displayed side-by-side with Greeks comparison table and payoff diagram.

## Scope & Safety

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Zero modifications to existing Phase 1–6 code** except:
> - Adding 1 route line in `server/src/app.js`
> - Adding `ML_SERVICE_URL` to `server/.env`
>
> All new code lives in isolated files/folders.

## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Python ML Service (`ml-service/`)

The existing `ml-service/` already has stub files (`app.py`, `utils/black_scholes.py`, `utils/greeks.py`, `models/hybrid_model.py`). We will **overwrite all of these** with the full implementations and **add new files**.

---

#### [MODIFY] [requirements.txt](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/requirements.txt)
- Replace with full dependency list: Flask 3.0.0, flask-cors 4.0.0, tensorflow 2.15.0, numpy, scipy, scikit-learn, joblib, pandas

#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/app.py)
- Complete Flask app with CORS for localhost:5000 and :5173
- Endpoints: `POST /predict`, `POST /train`, `GET /model-status`, `GET /health`
- All responses sanitized (no NaN/Infinity/null)
- Port 5001

#### [NEW] [models/black_scholes.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/models/black_scholes.py)
- Full analytical BS with all Greeks (Delta, Gamma, Theta, Vega, Rho)
- Boundary conditions enforced (T→0, σ→0 edge cases)
- All value clamping as specified

#### [NEW] [models/monte_carlo.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/models/monte_carlo.py)
- 10K simulations with antithetic variates
- Greeks via bump-and-reprice (finite difference) with shared random seed
- Returns std_error and 95% confidence interval

#### [MODIFY] [models/hybrid_model.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/models/hybrid_model.py)
- Full LSTM-CNN architecture (2×LSTM-64 + 1D-Conv-64 parallel branches, merged dense layers)
- Physics-informed loss: L_data + λ·L_PDE + γ·L_boundary
- Training with synthetic NSE data, Adam optimizer, early stopping
- Fallback to BS±5% noise when untrained

#### [NEW] [models/greeks.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/models/greeks.py)
- Numerical Greeks via finite difference (for MC and NN)

#### [NEW] [models/ensemble.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/models/ensemble.py)
- Weighted ensemble: 0.2×BS + 0.1×MC + 0.7×NN
- Boundary clamp on ensemble output

#### [NEW] [utils/validators.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/utils/validators.py)
- Input validation with strict bounds (S, K, T, r, sigma, option_type)
- Sanitization: convert to float, handle None/null

#### [NEW] [utils/feature_engineering.py](file:///c:/Users/Atul%20Patil/Desktop/Papertick/ml-service/utils/feature_engineering.py)
- 15 features from paper (log_moneyness, sqrt_T, d1, d2, bs_price, etc.)
- StandardScaler normalization
- Synthetic sequence generation (30 timesteps) for LSTM input

> [!NOTE]
> The old `ml-service/utils/black_scholes.py` and `ml-service/utils/greeks.py` will be kept as-is (they won't conflict since the new code imports from `models/`). If you prefer, I can delete them to avoid confusion.

